course: dictionary
lesson: 9490
title: Steel: a metal and a feeling
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Steel is a word with more than one job. It can be a noun for a strong metal, or a verb in the phrase steel yourself. The words around it show which meaning you need.
explain: «Most goods now cross the sea in standard steel boxes on giant ships.» Here steel is an adjective describing boxes, and it tells you the boxes are made of strong metal. «Carbon steel knives (not stainless) get dark spots when left wet» shows there are different kinds of steel.
explain: «She had to steel herself before she jumped.» Steel yourself does not mean turning into metal. It means making yourself brave and ready for something hard or scary. Try swapping in brave and ready: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Steel is made mostly from iron with a little carbon mixed in.
fact: Steel is very strong and hard, so we use it for bridges, cars, tools, pans and cutlery.
fact: Most steel is magnetic, so a magnet sticks to it.
fact: «Stainless steel» does not rust easily, which is why it is used for sinks and spoons.
fact: «To steel yourself» means to make yourself brave and ready for something hard or scary.
exercise: «Tall buildings became possible with steel frames and safe lifts.» In this sentence, what is steel? | A kind of soft cloth | A type of bird | *A strong metal used for building frames | To be very calm
exercise: «She had to steel herself before she jumped.» What does steel herself mean? | Fall asleep on the spot | *Make herself brave and ready | Paint herself silver | Melt into a puddle
exercise: «A fast train can need over a kilometre to stop, because steel wheels on steel rails have little grip.» Find and copy the word that names the metal. | grip | train | kilometre | *steel
test: «Stainless steel» is used for sinks and spoons because it... | *Does not rust easily | Is soft and bends easily | Gives out light | Is made of wood
test: Steel is mostly made from which metal? | Silver | Copper | Gold | *Iron
exam: Which fact about steel is true? | *Most steel is magnetic, so a magnet sticks to it | Steel is soft like a sponge | Steel floats on water like wood | Steel is made mostly from wax
